# Common Project Standards

## Naming (VoltPulse)

| Construct | Convention | Example |
|-----------|------------|---------|
| Apps / services | `pulse-*` or `grid-*` | `pulse-api`, `grid-perception` |
| Kafka topics | `vp.<domain>.*` | `vp.detect.v1` |
| Files TS/TSX | PascalCase components; kebab services | `FindingCard.tsx`, `alerts.service.ts` |
| Types / classes | PascalCase | `InspectionService` |
| Functions / vars | camelCase | `getFindingById` |
| DB columns | snake_case | `utility_id` |
| Env keys | SCREAMING_SNAKE | `PULSE_API_PORT` |

Detection enum: `crack | sag | corrosion | vegetation | thermal_hotspot`.  
Inspection status: `planned | in_progress | processing | review | closed | cancelled`.

## Config discipline

- Never hardcode hosts, ports, secrets, queue names, SLA timeouts, feature flags.
- Feature code reads `config` / settings objects — not raw `process.env` / `os.environ` sprinkled in business logic.
- Templates: `.env.template` tracked; real `.env` ignored.

## Errors

- Empty catch banned.
- API boundaries: typed DTOs; no raw ORM models out.
- Prefer minimal mutation responses (`{ id }`) unless contract says otherwise.

## Definition of done (any card)

- [ ] Acceptance criteria met
- [ ] Tests or smoke commands for changed behavior
- [ ] Evidence under card `evidence/`
- [ ] Anti-leak checklist clean for touched surfaces
- [ ] Formal `docs/` updated **only if** contract/arch/product decision changed
- [ ] No secrets in diff

## Right size

Implement card scope only. Extra abstractions need a new card or ADR.
